`verilator_config
// DD105-A Lab 06: the router's registers that the back door reaches.
//
// UVM's back door (peek, poke, and a write or read with UVM_BACKDOOR) finds a
// signal by its hierarchical name through VPI, and Verilator lets VPI see a
// signal only if it's marked public. These are the five flip-flop variables
// that hold CTRL, STATUS, INT_EN and DROP_CNT inside router_regs; the HDL
// paths in tb/router_ral_pkg.sv name them. The course's research found that
// the command-line flag that marks everything public (--public-flat-rw)
// breaks the UVM build on this simulator (5.050), so only these five are.
public_flat_rw -module "router_regs" -var "en_q"
public_flat_rw -module "router_regs" -var "status_q"
public_flat_rw -module "router_regs" -var "int_en_q"
public_flat_rw -module "router_regs" -var "cnt_noroute_q"
public_flat_rw -module "router_regs" -var "cnt_full_q"
